  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the number of ways to draw 12 segments of equal lengths such that each of the 24 vertices in a regular 24-gon is an endpoint of exactly one segment.\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution:\n\n1. **Understanding the Problem:**\n   - We have a regular 24-gon, which means it has 24 vertices labeled from 1 to 24.\n   - We need to draw 12 segments of equal lengths such that each vertex is an endpoint of exactly one segment.\n   - This means we need to pair up the vertices such that each vertex appears in exactly one segment.\n\n2. **Pairing Vertices:**\n   - Since we need to pair up 24 vertices, we need to find a way to pair them up such that each vertex is part of exactly one segment.\n   - This is equivalent to finding a perfect matching in a complete graph \\( K_{24} \\) where each vertex is paired with another vertex.\n\n3. **Perfect Matching:**\n   - A perfect matching in a complete graph \\( K_{24} \\) is a set of 12 edges such that each vertex is incident to exactly one edge.\n   - The number of perfect matchings in a complete graph \\( K_{2n} \\) is given by the double factorial of \\( (2n-1) \\), which is \\( (2n-1)!! \\).\n\n4. **Applying the Formula:**\n   - For \\( n = 12 \\) (since we have 24 vertices and we need 12 segments), the number of perfect matchings is given by:\n     \\[\n     (2 \\times 12 - 1)!! = 23!!\n     \\]\n   - The double factorial \\( 23!! \\) is the product of all odd numbers up to 23:\n     \\[\n     23!! = 23 \\times 21 \\times 19 \\times \\cdots \\times 3 \\times 1\n     \\]\n\n5. **Calculating the Double Factorial:**\n   - The double factorial \\( 23!! \\) can be calculated as follows:\n     \\[\n     23!! = 23 \\times 21 \\times 19 \\times 17 \\times 15 \\times 13 \\times 11 \\times 9 \\times 7 \\times 5 \\times 3 \\times 1\n     \\]\n   - This product is a large number, but it is the correct answer to the problem.\n\n### Final Answer:\nThe number of ways to draw 12 segments of equal lengths such that each vertex in a regular 24-gon is an endpoint of exactly one segment is given by the double factorial \\( 23!! \\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{23!!}\n\\]",
